- id: '2098731637378867500'
  text: 'GPT IMAGE 2.5 TURNED IMAGE GENERATION INTO VISUAL ENGINEERING.


    the prompt is no longer just a description of what to create.


    it is also a contract for what cannot change.


    i turned that system into a 50-page guide with 44 tested examples.


    for creation:


    → 24 adaptations of OpenAI’s prompting guide

    → 20 applications for app mockups, websites, product shots and thumbnails

    → one fictional brand carried across packaging, advertising, merchandise and a
    logo

    → reusable prompts for preserving its visual identity


    for control:


    → 6 text-heavy formats with exact copy + placement

    → a 50-element image map

    → one-arrow edits that protect 6 text strings, 5 tiers and 4 surrounding arrows

    → real failures: opaque cutouts, incorrect chart lengths and textures that changed
    when they shouldn’t


    the guide ends with one repeatable loop:


    inspect → specify → generate → review and repair → deliver


    plus a master prompt and portable skill for carrying the workflow into your next
    project.


    the breakthrough isn’t getting one beautiful image.


    it’s turning the picture in your head into instructions the model can execute,
    revise and preserve.


    save the system.'
