- id: '2079946571622326363'
  text: 'A reference sheet can now become a complete 3D asset and an interactive website.


    I generated the multi-view temple concept with GPT Image 2.0, then gave it to
    Codex + GPT-5.6 Ultra through Blender MCP.


    Blender was controlled entirely from the terminal. The model, materials, cameras,
    renders and exports were all generated through Python scripts. Codex then created
    a Three.js viewer where I can rotate the temple, switch between every angle and
    hide each architectural layer.


    The result still needs refinement, especially around the roofs and ornaments,
    but the complete image → Blender → web workflow is working.


    All from one prompt 👇'
